- Reset to Defaults: a left-aligned button in the bottom row restores every control on the dialog to its model default (after a confirm). Nothing persists until OK. The Toolbar tab resets to Restart-only

- The welcome card is the extension's own startup banner (v88.0) — `ShowChatWelcome(workspace)` → `ChatTranscript.ShowWelcome(title, facts, tips)`. Native mode never sees the CLI's greeting: the agent runs headless and its banner is not part of the event stream, so an empty transcript said nothing about what was running. Shown from exactly two places — after `session.StartAsync` in `TryStartNativeModeAsync`, and at the end of `RelaunchNativeSessionAsync` only when `forceNewSession`, since a model or permission switch keeps the conversation and a fresh-start card mid-thread would read as if it had been thrown away. It sits above `MessagesList` (not layered over it, which would cover the first answer) in its own `WelcomeScroll` ScrollViewer whose `MaxHeight` is bound to `TranscriptArea.ActualHeight` (v294.0): the `Auto` row measures the card with unlimited height, so a card taller than the tab (recent list + expanded tips) was cut off with no way to scroll and is dropped by `OnMessagesChanged` on the first `IsUser` row — not on the first row of any kind, or the "New chat" notice posted by the same relaunch would erase it immediately. `Clear()` hides it, leaving the caller to decide whether a new conversation is starting. Narrow tabs (v244.0): the left (mascot/facts) column stays `Auto` at its natural width; once the tips beside it would wrap so far that they are more than `WelcomeCardLayout.StackHeightRatio` (1.2) times as tall as that column is wide (`WelcomeCardLayout.ShouldStack`; the tips' height, not the card's — a tall left column is not helped by stacking), `ApplyWelcomeLayout` moves the tips into row 2 under a horizontal divider. With the recent list shown (below) the height test is skipped — the list stays beside the facts whatever its height, and only a column with no room at all (`TipsWidth <= 0`) still stacks. `RefreshWelcomeLayout` probes the *side-by-side* height — `Measure` of the left panel unconstrained and of the tips panel at `TipsWidth`, margins swapped for the side-by-side ones — never the current height: stacked, the tips are much shorter, so testing that would flip the card back and forth. Because the probe is hypothetical it is idempotent, so it runs on every `SizeChanged` (height too — zoom, new content) and the flip's own resize settles in one pass; it is deferred to `DispatcherPriority.Loaded` since it measures, and ends with `InvalidateMeasure` so the grid re-measures the probed panels with its real constraints. The "Signed in as Name (email)" fact is the longest line, so `ShowChatWelcome` passes it through `WelcomeCardLayout.BreakBeforeEmail`, which moves a trailing `(…@…)` onto its own line (the facts are plain `TextBlock`s, so `\n` is a line break); the transcript notice with the same text is left on one line. Recent conversations (v276.0): for a Claude provider `ShowChatWelcome` also calls `BeginWelcomeRecentSessionsLookup`, which reads the workspace's newest transcripts in the background (`LoadRecentClaudeSessionsAsync`: files by mtime, parsed only until `WelcomeRecentSessionCount` = 5 with at least one prompt are found; name = transcript title, else the saved one) and hands rows to `ChatTranscriptView.SetWelcomeRecentSessions`. With rows, the right column (`WelcomeTipsPanel`) shows `WelcomeRecentPanel` and folds the tips (`WelcomeTipsSection`) behind a "Show tips" link (`_welcomeTipsExpanded`, reset by `HideWelcome`, never saved); no rows or another agent → tips as before. The list survives `ShowWelcome` re-renders (version/account lookups); `_welcomeRecentLookups` stops those re-renders from starting parallel reads, and the result is applied only while the card is still visible. Since v276.0 sessions open in a chat tab are no longer skipped (the card then disagreed with Session History): `TryFindOpenChatTab` (matches `SessionId` or `ResumableSessionId` of `_agentSession` and every `_nativeSessions` entry) adds "already open" to the row, and a click on such a row brings that tab forward (`Switch